Task 4: Food Delivery Home Screen

Build a styled Flutter home screen for a food delivery app that combines layout widgets,app-wide theming and navigation to a restaurant 
detail screen.

->Create a MaterialApp with a ThemeData that sets a primary colour, an accent colour and a default text style; apply it to a Scaffold 
with an AppBar titled 'QuickBite'.
->Use Row, Column and Container widgets with explicit padding and margin to build a restaurant card that shows an icon placeholder, 
restaurant name and a star rating text.
->Add an ElevatedButton labelled 'View Menu' that uses Navigator.push to open a RestaurantDetailScreen.
->Pass the restaurant name as a constructor argument to RestaurantDetailScreen and display it in that screen's AppBar title and body.

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(QuickBiteApp());
}

class QuickBiteApp extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,
      title: 'QuickBite',
      theme: ThemeData(
        colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(
          seedColor: Color(0xFFB71C1C),
        ),
        scaffoldBackgroundColor: Color(0xFFFFF8F0),
        appBarTheme: AppBarTheme(
          backgroundColor: Color(0xFFB71C1C),
          foregroundColor: Colors.white,
        ),
        elevatedButtonTheme: ElevatedButtonThemeData(
          style: ElevatedButton.styleFrom(
            backgroundColor: Color(0xFFB71C1C),
            foregroundColor: Colors.white,
            padding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(
              horizontal: 18,
              vertical: 12,
            ),
          ),
        ),
        useMaterial3: true,
      ),
      home: HomeScreen(),
    );
  }
}

